## What Problem This Solves

ClawRouter's bundled native plugin did not register an image-generation provider, so native image requests failed before reaching its JSON Images API.

## User Impact

Users with entitled ClawRouter image models can select qualified flare/sunburst models through native image runtime, tool, CLI, and discovery surfaces. The service generation route must be deployed before live use; this change does not deploy it or grant access.

## Why This Change Was Made

- Register a generation-only plugin provider with fresh same-key catalog validation. Preserve actual qualified model IDs and supported dated snapshots; choose defaults only from eligible authorized catalog rows, never an absent direct-OpenAI default.
- Resolve scoped/profile-aware ClawRouter credentials through the public SDK. Use the same key for catalog and generation, without upstream OpenAI key fallback. Unknown, failed, empty, or ineligible catalogs cannot authorize generation.
- Enforce offered prompt/count/size bounds; reject unsupported edits, reference inputs, masks, variations, and streaming rather than advertising them.
- Reuse public guarded HTTP, deadline/cancellation, bounded asset parsing, MIME sniffing, and safe result download helpers. Forward an optional caller AbortSignal through the shared image runtime and compatible HTTP/download paths.
- Honor existing explicit private-network policy, environment proxies, and caller-selected deadlines across catalog lookup, generation, and result download. Do not forward provider credentials to result-storage origins.

No service code, primary/fallback routing, global auth/default/Fast bindings, or unrelated provider capability changes. Narrow plugin registration edits can compose with the separate speech/image-understanding branches.

