## What Problem This Solves

Fixes PostgreSQL-backed agents being refused during deferred Gateway startup with `Agent <id> was deleted during startup inspection` even when the deletion journal is empty.

## User Impact

Configured agents can finish startup and load their model authentication. A deletion committed after the database opens still prevents authentication publication. No configuration changes or data migration are required.

## Why This Change Was Made

The native auth reader sends a separate admission request when transferring its rows. That request omitted the deletion-journal fact required by startup admission, so the host treated an unknown status as a refusal. The auth operation now reads that fact from its existing execution owner immediately before publication. The host guard and deletion semantics are unchanged.

## Evidence

- Reproduced the false refusal at the native worker admission boundary before fixing the producer.
- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/state/agent-deletion-journal.native-startup.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: **5/5 passed** on this upstream branch (16.07 s test lane; 53.28 s including cold worker compilation). Coverage includes cold startup, successful auth publication with an empty journal, and refusal when deletion arrives between open and auth publication.
- Core typecheck passed through `scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json`.
- Targeted native lint with `config/tsconfig/oxlint.core.json`, formatting, and `git diff --check` passed.
- Fresh independent review of this upstream-only patch and its native guard/auth-reader context found no actionable P0/P1 issues.

