## What Problem This Solves

Doctor and update-time config migration replace explicitly selected, still-served OpenAI models with newer generations. For example, `openai/gpt-4.1-mini` becomes `openai/gpt-5.4-mini`, including its saved alias/settings and fallback selections.

## User Impact

Canonical `openai/*` choices now survive Doctor unless the OpenAI plugin declares a completed retirement for the selected endpoint. Confirmed API retirements still migrate through the existing route/auth/successor checks; custom endpoints keep their model IDs. No new setting is needed.

This PR is scoped to the canonical OpenAI provider. Legacy `openai-codex`, Copilot, Claude, xAI, and Groq substitutions remain separate follow-up work, so it does not close the full cross-provider issue.

## Why This Change Was Made

Remove canonical OpenAI from the unconditional legacy-generation substitution table. Declare the eight already-shut-down API IDs in the existing OpenAI manifest retirement metadata, scoped to `api.openai.com`, using the provider's documented successors. Keep the GPT-5.6 spelling normalization and existing ChatGPT-route retirements.

The [OpenAI deprecation history](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/deprecations) records seven of these shutdowns on July 23, 2026 and `gpt-5.2-chat-latest` on August 10, 2026. Models with future shutdown dates are deliberately not retired early. Existing billing-warning coverage now uses an actually retired model instead of relying on the reported GPT-4o Mini bug.

## Evidence

Real `pnpm openclaw --profile doctor-model-proof doctor --fix --non-interactive` runs on macOS 27.0 / Node 26.4.0, with task-owned state and synthetic credentials:

| Case | Observed result |
| --- | --- |
| Active primary + fallbacks | Baseline changed `gpt-4.1-mini` to `gpt-5.4-mini`, and `gpt-4o`/`gpt-5.1` to `gpt-5.5`. Candidate preserves the original primary, ordered fallbacks, alias and runtime settings across two runs. |
| Retired API model | Candidate migrates `gpt-5-chat-latest` to documented `gpt-5.6-sol` on `api.openai.com`. |
| Same ID on custom endpoint | Candidate preserves `gpt-5-chat-latest`. |
| No applicable account/endpoint evidence | Candidate preserves `gpt-5-chat-latest` and reports that its exact authentication route is unavailable. |

The new preservation regression failed on baseline for the exact unwanted substitutions. Three new manifest route cases failed before the retirement metadata was added. All 107 focused migration, route-suppression, successor-guard, billing and deferred-update tests pass.

Per-file single-worker wall time (`pnpm test <file> --maxWorkers=1`):

- `legacy-config-migrate.media-models.test.ts`: 11.95 s.
- `legacy-config-migrate.test.ts`: 26.18 s.
- `manifest-model-suppression.test.ts`: 7.65 s.
- `doctor-config-flow.billing-route.test.ts`: 126.19 s through the repository runner. Its existing six cases exercise persisted config/auth decisions, billing warnings, deferred update receipts, reloaded idempotency and write refusals; this patch adds no process boots or test cases there.

The published stable installed-updater proof has now passed on the exact PR commit; inspectable captures are included below. Authenticated model inference was not run. Update-time deferral and durable completion are also covered by the existing Doctor flow tests. The initial draft PR run skipped the build/test matrix; CI test seconds are unavailable until those jobs execute.

Validation: core production typecheck, extension production/test typechecks, targeted lint, formatting, focused tests and one P0–P2 autoreview pass passed. Autoreview found no actionable issues.

`check:changed` stopped at an unrelated core-test type error: `src/agents/main-session-recovery/main-session-restart-recovery-admission.test.ts:705` passes `{ title: "preparation progress" }` to `patchSessionEntryCore`, but `InternalSessionEntry` has no `title` field. Both the test and session-entry type are unchanged from base `2009aa6c26a91b66111ab8bed53623eb115163d2`. All preceding selected checks passed; the aggregate check is not green. No unrelated source changes or CI reruns were made.



